@namespace AuthWithAdmin.Client.Pages.ProjectWorkspace
@using AuthWithAdmin.Shared.AuthSharedModels
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Services
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Components
@inject IProjectWorkspaceService Workspace

@*
    ProjectResourcesSection — "משאבי הפרויקט"

    The team's own working links: the spec doc, the Drive folder, the Figma
    file, the repo. Deliberately lightweight — this is quick access to what the
    team already uses, not a document management system. Course material stays
    where it belongs, in מרכז ידע.

    Visual language: ONE card holding an APPLICATION-FOLDER GRID — a fluid
    wall of small tiles, each a mark above a label above a quiet type line,
    the way an OS shows a folder of apps. Each tile is a real <a>, so keyboard
    activation and the browser's own affordances come for free.

    The marks are painted by the shared #motivaIconGradient paint server
    (AppLayout) through .motiva-ico-gradient — no tinted chip, no flat violet.
    That is the product's one icon treatment, not a second one invented here.

    ── EACH RESOURCE MAY BELONG TO A DELIVERABLE ─────────────────────────────
    The form's third field associates a resource with one of תוצרי ההגשה
    (ProjectResources.DeliverableKey). It is OPTIONAL and defaults to none — a
    resource that belongs to the project as a whole is still the ordinary case.

    That single association is what lets תוצרי ההגשה derive "בעבודה" from real
    data: a deliverable with at least one associated resource is being worked
    on, and nobody has to say so in a second place. The tile states the
    association on its type line, so the thing driving a deliverable's state is
    visible from here too.

    ── ONE FORM, TWO JOBS, ONE DIALOG ────────────────────────────────────────
    Adding and editing are the same three fields, so they are the same fragment
    (ResourceForm below) in the same place: a modal. Nothing about the
    interaction differs between them except the button words and the presence
    of "הסרה".

    IT USED TO BE INLINE — above the grid when adding, and in the edited tile's
    own place when editing — and that is what changed. Both positions grew the
    card: this card is the bottom half of the page's right column and takes that
    column's height, so an expanding form either pushed the tile wall into an
    internal scroll or resized one column of the row while the other stayed put.
    The same reason the project card's editor became a dialog, and the same
    shell: MModal, Size.Medium. See ProjectIdentityEditModal for the full
    argument.

    ── WHY THE TILE CARRIES ONLY A PENCIL ────────────────────────────────────
    The tile's primary action is opening the resource, and it stays the whole
    tile. The pencil is the only thing layered on top of that: one 22px control
    in the tile's top corner, invisible at rest, revealed on hover and on
    keyboard focus. It sits clear of the centred mark and label, so it covers
    nothing. Deleting moved OUT of the tile and into the editor — a destructive
    one-click control on a hover-revealed corner button was both the busiest
    thing on the tile and the easiest to hit by accident.

    One deliberate departure from the design export:
      * ONE ACCENT for every kind. The Master permits three semantic colours and
        none of these is a status, so the kind is carried by the icon instead.
        See ProjectResourceKinds.
*@

@*
    THE CARD IS THE SECTION, AND IT SITS UNDER THE PROJECT CARD.

    Its position has moved twice for the same reason each time — where the tile
    wall has the width it needs without leaving a hole elsewhere. As the left
    column of a 50/50 row it was a two-tile-wide list; full width below both
    columns it read fine but left the bottom of the right column empty once
    תוצרי ההגשה took that column. It now occupies exactly that space: second in
    the right column's vertical stack, at ~57% of the content width, which is
    still five or six tiles to a row.

    What the card DID settle stays settled: "+ הוספת משאב" lives in the card's
    own head, beside the heading it belongs to, rather than alone at the far
    edge of a bare section.
*@
@* `Fill`: this card is the bottom half of the page's right column, and that
   column is as tall as תוצרי ההגשה beside it — see .pw-col-project in
   ProjectWorkspacePage.razor.css. Fill is the one way a caller can reach an
   MCard's root across CSS isolation, and it gives the card its cell's height
   plus the flex column that lets the tile wall below the head scroll instead
   of spilling out of the card. *@
@*  THE ONE MOUNT POINT for the add/edit dialog. `_editingId` decides which
    of its two jobs it is doing; IsFormOpen decides whether it exists at all,
    so the shell is torn down on close and its scroll lock released with it. *@
@if (IsFormOpen)
{
    @ResourceForm(_editingId is not null)
}

<MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Fill="true">
<section class="pwr" aria-labelledby="pwr-heading">

    <div class="pwr-head">
        <div class="pwr-headtext">
            <h2 class="pwr-heading" id="pwr-heading">משאבי הפרויקט</h2>
            <p class="pwr-sub">הקישורים והכלים שהצוות עובד איתם</p>
        </div>

        @* Primary: adding a resource is this section's create action, so it
           takes the shared gradient CTA like every other add/create in the
           workspace.

           IT IS IN THE HEAD WHETHER OR NOT THE TEAM HAS RESOURCES YET. It used
           to be gated on `_resources.Count > 0`, with a SECOND copy of the same
           button inside the empty state below — so the one case where adding a
           resource is the only thing to do was the one case where the section's
           own action was missing from its head, and the page carried two
           controls for one job. One button, one place, always. *@
        @*  Unconditional now. It used to be hidden while the inline form was
            open, because the form appeared directly beneath it and the button
            would have offered to open what was already open. The form is a
            dialog over the page, so the head simply stays as it is.  *@
        <MButton Variant="MButton.ButtonVariant.Primary"
                 Size="MButton.ButtonSize.Small"
                 OnClick="StartAdd">
            + הוספת משאב
        </MButton>
    </div>

    @* Outside the form on purpose: a failed DELETE has to be able to report
       itself too, and it can happen while no form is open. *@
    @if (_error is not null)
    {
        <p class="pwr-error" role="alert">@_error</p>
    }

    @if (Loading)
    {
        <p class="pwr-note" role="status" aria-live="polite">טוענת משאבים…</p>
    }
    else if (LoadFailed)
    {
        <p class="pwr-note pwr-note-error" role="status">
            לא הצלחנו לטעון את משאבי הפרויקט.
        </p>
    }
    else if (Resources.Count == 0)
    {
        @* ONE LINE, NOT A PANEL.

               This was an MEmptyState: a centred title, a two-line explanation
               and a button, ~170px of reserved height under .motiva-final. On a
               page of four stacked sections that is not an empty state, it is a
               hole — and everything it said was already on the screen. The
               title restated the heading two rows up, the description restated
               `.pwr-sub` ("הקישורים והכלים שהצוות עובד איתם") directly beneath
               it, and the button is now permanently in the head.

               So the section collapses to its head plus one quiet line, and
               nothing is lost: the wording, the action and the reading order
               are all still here, in less than a fifth of the height.

               `.pwr-note` is the class the loading and load-failed lines beside
               it already use — same register, same rhythm, no new declaration
               for a third way of saying "there is nothing here yet". *@
        <p class="pwr-note">עדיין לא נוספו משאבים.</p>
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="pwr-grid">
            @foreach (var resource in Resources)
            {
                var captured = resource;

                @*  Every resource is a tile, always. Editing used to replace
                    the edited tile with the form in its own place; the form is
                    a dialog now, so the wall never rearranges itself and the
                    tile stays visible behind the thing editing it.  *@
                {
                    var kind = ProjectResourceKinds.Detect(captured.Url);
                    var host = ProjectResourceKinds.HostOf(captured.Url);

                    @* AN APP TILE: mark above label, centred, in a fluid
                       grid — the Applications-folder arrangement, drawn in
                       Motiva's own language rather than macOS's.

                       The horizontal rectangle it replaces put the mark, the
                       name and the type on one line, which is a LIST ROW with
                       a border around it however wide the track is. Stacking
                       them is what makes a wall of these scannable by mark
                       first, which is the whole point of an app folder.

                       Still one real <a>, still the whole hit area. *@
                    <div class="pwr-cell">
                        <a class="pwr-hit"
                           href="@captured.Url"
                           target="_blank"
                           rel="noopener noreferrer"
                           title="@(host ?? captured.Url)">
                            @* The shared paint server, not a flat violet: the
                               gradient is ON THE STROKE, with no tinted chip
                               behind it — the treatment .motiva-ico-gradient
                               documents in motiva-base.css, and the same one
                               every card-head glyph in the product uses. At
                               26px the sweep reads as all three hues; the
                               13px doc chips inside a deliverable deliberately
                               keep flat ink, because below ~12px this gradient
                               collapses to its blue midpoint. *@
                            <span class="pwr-icon motiva-ico-gradient" aria-hidden="true">
                                <svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                     stroke="url(#motivaIconGradient)" stroke-width="1.5"
                                     stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                    <path d="@ProjectResourceKinds.IconPath(kind)"></path>
                                </svg>
                            </span>
                            <span class="pwr-text">
                                <span class="pwr-title">@captured.Label</span>
                                <span class="pwr-type">@ProjectResourceKinds.Label(kind)</span>

                                @* The association, stated where it is made.
                                   A separate line rather than appended to the
                                   type: the type is derived from the URL and
                                   the deliverable is a decision the team took,
                                   and running them together as
                                   "Figma · דף מידע" reads as one fact when it
                                   is two. Rendered only when the key still
                                   matches a catalog entry, so a renamed key
                                   goes quiet instead of printing a raw slug. *@
                                @if (DeliverableTitleOf(captured) is { } deliverableTitle)
                                {
                                    <span class="pwr-tag">
                                        <span class="pwr-tag-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                        @deliverableTitle
                                    </span>
                                }
                            </span>
                        </a>

                        @* Sibling of the anchor, never a child: a button inside
                           a link is invalid markup and unreachable by keyboard.
                           It sits in the gutter .pwr-hit reserves, so it can
                           never cover the label. *@
                        <button type="button"
                                class="pwr-edit"
                                title="עריכת המשאב"
                                aria-label="@($"עריכת המשאב {captured.Label}")"
                                @onclick="() => StartEdit(captured)">
                            <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                                 stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                                <path d="M12 20h9"></path>
                                <path d="M16.5 3.5a2.12 2.12 0 0 1 3 3L7 19l-4 1 1-4Z"></path>
                            </svg>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                }
            }
        </div>
    }

</section>
</MCard>

@code {
    private const int MaxLabel = 80;
    private const int MaxUrl   = 2000;

    // ── THE LIST IS THE PAGE'S, NOT THIS SECTION'S ───────────────────────
    // תוצרי ההגשה reads the same resources to derive its "בעבודה" state, so
    // one owner (ProjectWorkspacePage) loads them once and both consumers
    // render from that single list. This section still performs every WRITE —
    // it owns the form — and reports the outcome upwards, which is what keeps
    // the deliverable panel in step with an edit made down here without a
    // refetch.
    [Parameter] public IReadOnlyList<ProjectResourceDto> Resources { get; set; }
        = Array.Empty<ProjectResourceDto>();

    /// <summary>The page's read is still in flight.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Loading { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The page's read FAILED — a different screen from "no resources
    /// yet", which is an empty list.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool LoadFailed { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public EventCallback<ProjectResourceDto> OnAdded   { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<ProjectResourceDto> OnUpdated { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<int>                OnRemoved { get; set; }

    private bool   _adding;
    private int?   _editingId;
    private bool   _saving;
    private bool   _deleting;
    private string _labelDraft = "";
    private string _urlDraft   = "";

    /// <summary>The deliverable the open form will associate its resource with.
    /// Empty string is "no association" — the <select>'s first option — and is
    /// what gets sent as null.</summary>
    private string _deliverableDraft = "";

    private string? _error;

    /// <summary>The label field of whichever form is open, so it can take focus
    /// the moment the form appears.</summary>
    private ElementReference _labelInput;
    private bool             _focusPending;

    private bool IsFormOpen => _adding || _editingId is not null;

    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<MSelect.Option> DeliverableOptions =
        new[] { new MSelect.Option("", "ללא שיוך — משאב כללי של הפרויקט") }
            .Concat(SubmissionDeliverablesCatalog.All.Select(d => new MSelect.Option(d.Key, d.Title)))
            .ToList();

    /// <summary>Whether any write is in flight — both buttons and both fields
    /// disable together, so a form can never be submitted twice or cancelled
    /// out from under a request.</summary>
    private bool IsBusy => _saving || _deleting;

    // ── The form ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // One definition for add and edit. `isEdit` changes the button words and
    // adds "הסרה"; everything else — fields, keys, validation, error surface —
    // is deliberately identical, because to the student it is the same act.
    //
    // THE SHELL IS MModal, UNMODIFIED — the same one ProjectIdentityEditModal
    // uses, at the same Size.Medium that `.motiva-final` scopes to the finished
    // student geometry (460px, radius-xl, soft ink scrim, the continuous
    // 26/28px pad, no divider rules). Rendering it here rather than wrapping it
    // in a second component is deliberate: this section owns every write, the
    // drafts and the error surface, and a component boundary between the form
    // and its state would only have to pass all of it back and forth. Nothing
    // about the create/update/delete logic changed.
    //
    // FitContent stays OFF, as on the project dialog: a form wants the default,
    // where the dialog is capped at the viewport and `.m-modal-body` scrolls
    // with the header and footer pinned.
    private RenderFragment ResourceForm(bool isEdit) =>@<MModal IsOpen="true"
            Size="MModal.ModalSize.Medium"
            Title="@(isEdit ? "עריכת משאב" : "הוספת משאב")"
            Class="pwr-modal"
            OnClose="CloseForm">

        <ChildContent>
            <div class="pwr-field">
                <label class="pwr-fieldlabel" for="pwr-label">שם המשאב</label>
                <input id="pwr-label"
                       class="pwr-input"
                       type="text"
                       maxlength="@MaxLabel"
                       placeholder="לדוגמה: מסמך האפיון"
                       disabled="@IsBusy"
                       @ref="_labelInput"
                       @bind="_labelDraft"
                       @bind:event="oninput"
                       @onkeydown="HandleFormKeyDownAsync" />
            </div>

            @* dir="ltr" on the URL field only: a pasted link is Latin text and
               reads backwards inside an RTL field. The label above it stays
               RTL — this is a per-field property, not a page one. *@
            <div class="pwr-field">
                <label class="pwr-fieldlabel" for="pwr-url">קישור</label>
                <input id="pwr-url"
                       class="pwr-input"
                       type="url"
                       dir="ltr"
                       maxlength="@MaxUrl"
                       placeholder="https://…"
                       disabled="@IsBusy"
                       @bind="_urlDraft"
                       @bind:event="oninput"
                       @onkeydown="HandleFormKeyDownAsync" />

                @* The kind is DERIVED from the URL, never stored, so it cannot
                   be edited directly — it changes when the link changes.
                   Showing it live while the link is typed is what makes that
                   rule visible instead of mysterious. It sits under the field
                   it describes now, rather than at the foot of the form. *@
                @if (DetectedKindLabel is { } kindLabel)
                {
                    <p class="pwr-kindhint">סוג: <strong>@kindLabel</strong> · נקבע אוטומטית לפי הקישור</p>
                }
            </div>

            @* THE ASSOCIATION — optional, and last, because it is the only
               field that is not about the link itself.

               The value is the catalog KEY; only the title is ever shown. That
               is the same key ProjectSubmissionStatuses stores, so an artifact
               and a declared status are keyed identically. *@
            <div class="pwr-field">
                @*  The consequence of choosing a deliverable used to be a
                    permanent two-line sentence under the select. It is worth
                    saying — it explains a state change the student does not
                    otherwise trigger — and it is not worth standing space in a
                    three-field dialog, which is what MInfoTip is for.  *@
                @*  THE TIP LEADS THE ROW, and that is geometry rather than
                    taste. The bubble is anchored at its trigger's inline-start
                    and grows toward the inline-end — leftward under RTL — up to
                    340px. Placed AFTER the label it starts one label-width in
                    from the dialog's right edge, so on a long label like this
                    one it ran past the left edge and was clipped. Leading the
                    row puts its anchor at the body's own start edge, where the
                    full 443px is available and any label length fits.

                    SINGLE-quoted attribute, so the sentence keeps its real
                    double quotes around "בעבודה": a Razor attribute value is a
                    C# string, not markup, so &quot; inside a double-quoted one
                    is passed through as those six literal characters.  *@
                <div class="pwr-labelrow">
                    <MInfoTip Text='משאב שמשויך לתוצר מסמן אותו אוטומטית כ"בעבודה", עד שהתוצר מסומן כהושלם.'
                              TriggerLabel="מידע על שיוך לתוצר הגשה"
                              Placement="MInfoTip.TipPlacement.Above" />
                    <label class="pwr-fieldlabel" for="pwr-deliverable">שיוך לתוצר הגשה (רשות)</label>
                </div>
                <MSelectField Options="@DeliverableOptions"
                              @bind-Value="_deliverableDraft"
                              Disabled="@IsBusy"
                              Class="pwr-select" />
            </div>

            @if (_error is not null)
            {
                <p class="pwr-formerror" role="alert">@_error</p>
            }

            @if (isEdit)
            {
                @*  DESTRUCTIVE, AND NOT IN THE FOOTER. The footer carries the
                    one primary action and nothing else; a delete beside a save
                    is the classic mis-click. It stays where this component
                    already decided it belongs — one step inside the flow, as
                    the quietest control on the surface — which is also why it
                    is not on the tile any more.  *@
                <div class="pwr-danger">
                    <MButton Variant="MButton.ButtonVariant.Ghost"
                             Size="MButton.ButtonSize.Small"
                             Class="pwr-remove"
                             Loading="_deleting"
                             LoadingText="מסירה…"
                             Disabled="_saving"
                             OnClick="DeleteEditedAsync">
                        הסרת המשאב
                    </MButton>
                </div>
            }
        </ChildContent>

        <FooterContent>
            @*  ONE ACTION. The dialog's X is the secondary exit — a footer
                ביטול beside it would be two controls for one job, and the
                shell's own `justify-content: flex-end` already puts this on
                the physical left under RTL.  *@
            <MButton Variant="MButton.ButtonVariant.Primary"
                     Size="MButton.ButtonSize.Small"
                     Loading="_saving"
                     LoadingText="@(isEdit ? "שומרת…" : "מוסיפה…")"
                     Disabled="_deleting"
                     OnClick="SaveFormAsync">
                @(isEdit ? "שמירה" : "הוספה")
            </MButton>
        </FooterContent>
    </MModal>;

    // NO LOAD HERE. ProjectWorkspacePage reads api/projects/my-resources once
    // and passes the result in — see the Resources parameter above.

    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (!_focusPending) return;

        _focusPending = false;
        // Best-effort: a form that has just been closed again by a fast second
        // click leaves nothing to focus, and that is not an error.
        try { await _labelInput.FocusAsync(); } catch { }
    }

    private string? DetectedKindLabel =>
        string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_urlDraft)
            ? null
            : ProjectResourceKinds.Label(ProjectResourceKinds.Detect(NormalizedDraftUrl));

    /// <summary>What the server will store, for the kind hint only: a bare host
    /// is upgraded to https there, so the hint has to judge the same string the
    /// card will end up rendering.</summary>
    private string NormalizedDraftUrl
    {
        get
        {
            var url = (_urlDraft ?? "").Trim();
            return url.Contains("://", StringComparison.Ordinal) ? url : $"https://{url}";
        }
    }

    // ── Open / close ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private void StartAdd()
    {
        _adding           = true;
        _editingId        = null;
        _labelDraft       = "";
        _urlDraft         = "";
        _deliverableDraft = "";
        _error            = null;
        _focusPending     = true;
    }

    private void StartEdit(ProjectResourceDto resource)
    {
        _adding           = false;
        _editingId        = resource.Id;
        _labelDraft       = resource.Label;
        _urlDraft         = resource.Url;
        // A key that no longer matches a catalog entry would select nothing and
        // then be SAVED BACK as "no association" by the next edit. Dropping it
        // to empty here makes that explicit instead of accidental.
        _deliverableDraft = KnownDeliverableKey(resource.DeliverableKey) ?? "";
        _error            = null;
        _focusPending     = true;
    }

    /// <summary>The catalog key if it still exists, else null. One place where
    /// an unknown key is judged, used by both the tile and the editor.</summary>
    private static string? KnownDeliverableKey(string? key) =>
        string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(key)
            ? null
            : SubmissionDeliverablesCatalog.All.Any(d => d.Key == key) ? key : null;

    /// <summary>The deliverable's TITLE for a tile's tag line, or null when the
    /// resource is unassociated or carries a key the catalog no longer has.</summary>
    private static string? DeliverableTitleOf(ProjectResourceDto resource) =>
        SubmissionDeliverablesCatalog.All
            .FirstOrDefault(d => d.Key == resource.DeliverableKey)?.Title;

    private void CloseForm()
    {
        _adding    = false;
        _editingId = null;
        _error     = null;
    }

    private async Task HandleFormKeyDownAsync(KeyboardEventArgs e)
    {
        if (e.Key == "Enter")       await SaveFormAsync();
        else if (e.Key == "Escape") CloseForm();
    }

    // ── Write ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task SaveFormAsync()
    {
        if (IsBusy) return;

        var label = (_labelDraft ?? "").Trim();
        var url   = (_urlDraft   ?? "").Trim();

        // Both checks mirror the server's own, so the common mistakes are
        // answered without a round trip. The server still validates — this is
        // convenience, not the boundary.
        if (label.Length == 0)
        {
            _error = "יש להזין שם למשאב.";
            return;
        }

        if (url.Length == 0)
        {
            _error = "יש להזין קישור.";
            return;
        }

        // Empty select → no association. Sent as null, which is also what
        // CLEARS an existing association on an edit.
        var deliverableKey = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_deliverableDraft)
            ? null
            : _deliverableDraft;

        _saving = true;
        _error  = null;

        if (_editingId is { } id)
        {
            var updated = await Workspace.UpdateResourceAsync(id, label, url, deliverableKey);
            _saving = false;

            if (updated is null)
            {
                _error = "שמירת המשאב נכשלה. ודאי שהקישור מתחיל ב-http או ב-https ונסי שנית.";
                return;
            }

            await OnUpdated.InvokeAsync(updated);
        }
        else
        {
            var created = await Workspace.AddResourceAsync(label, url, deliverableKey);
            _saving = false;

            if (created is null)
            {
                // The server rejects a non-http(s) URL with a 400, which is by
                // far the likeliest reason to land here.
                _error = "הוספת המשאב נכשלה. ודאי שהקישור מתחיל ב-http או ב-https ונסי שנית.";
                return;
            }

            await OnAdded.InvokeAsync(created);
        }

        CloseForm();
    }

    private async Task DeleteEditedAsync()
    {
        if (IsBusy || _editingId is not { } id) return;

        _deleting = true;
        _error    = null;

        var ok = await Workspace.DeleteResourceAsync(id);

        _deleting = false;

        if (!ok)
        {
            _error = "הסרת המשאב נכשלה. נסי שנית.";
            return;
        }

        await OnRemoved.InvokeAsync(id);
        CloseForm();
    }
}
